; host-exec-launch-honesty-band.fk — a host-exec whose sh NEVER LAUNCHED
; answers the axiom-1 nothing; "" is reserved for a command that RAN and spoke
; zero bytes. Before 2026-08-27 both answered "" (the silent-partial family on
; the exec side): under ulimit -u 100 with 485 live user procs, ten
; (host-exec "date +%s%N" "") calls answered ten empty strings rc 0, and
; observe/hot-crossing-run.fk's 10s await window silently closed in 0.008s
; (PR #542 diagnosis). This band starves fork for real — ulimit -u 1 in the
; door shell, exec so no fork stands between the limit and the probe — and
; reads the distinction from inside the starved kernel via
; observe/host-exec-starved-probe.fk.
;
; PROOF LEVEL: FOURTH-ARM ONLY — host-exec binds on go and fkwu (pf-arm-mask
; 9), and the starvation leg drives the repo-root fkwu binary itself, so this
; band runs on its home arm:
;   ./fkwu form/form-stdlib/tests/host-exec-launch-honesty-band.fk
; The Go arm's twin witness is TestHostExecLaunchFailureAnswersNothing
; (form/form-kernel-go/hostexec_test.go). jitabi carries no host-exec seat —
; the Go JIT leaves natives to the interpreter ("Natives we don't support in
; the compiled body", jit.go) — so the two heals cover every seat.
;
; Bits (power-of-two weights):
;   1  empty speech stays a string: (host-exec "printf ''") is NOT nothing, len 0
;   2  real speech crosses: (host-exec "printf hx-tok") answers "hx-tok"
;   4  starved launch answers nothing (probe token tens digit = 1)
;   8  str_len of that starved nothing still answers 0 (probe ones digit = 1)
; witnessed: 2026-08-27 -> 15
(do
    (defn hxb-digit? (b) (if (and (ge b 48) (le b 57)) 1 0))
    (defn hxb-int (s i n acc)
        (if (ge i n) acc
            (do (let b (str_byte_at s i))
                (if (eq (hxb-digit? b) 1)
                    (hxb-int s (add i 1) n (add (mul acc 10) (sub b 48)))
                    acc))))

    (let r0 (host-exec "printf ''" ""))
    (let c0 (if (and (eq (nothing? r0) 0) (eq (str_len r0) 0)) 1 0))

    (let r1 (host-exec "printf hx-tok" ""))
    (let c1 (if (eq (str_eq r1 "hx-tok") 1) 2 0))

    (let tok (host-exec
        "ulimit -u 1; exec ./fkwu observe/host-exec-starved-probe.fk 2>/dev/null" ""))
    (let n (if (nothing? tok) 0 (hxb-int tok 0 (str_len tok) 0)))
    (let c2 (if (eq (div n 10) 1) 4 0))
    (let c3 (if (and (eq (div n 10) 1) (eq (mod n 10) 1)) 8 0))

    (add c0 (add c1 (add c2 c3))))
